Apple today quietly introduced updated Magic Keyboard models with revised U.S. English key labeling.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/apple-magic-keyboard-with-glyphs-2026-refresh.png" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1060954" /><br/>
On the new keyboards, the tab, caps lock, shift, return, and delete keycaps are labeled with glyphs rather than edge text. On the full-size models with a numeric keypad, the change goes further, with the home, page up, page down, end, clear, and enter keys also swapping their text labels for symbols.<br/>
<br/>
Four models have been updated: the <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mjlx4ll/a/magic-keyboard-usb-c-us-english">Magic Keyboard</a>, the <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mjly4ll/a/magic-keyboard-with-touch-id-for-mac-models-with-apple-silicon-usb-c-us-english">Magic Keyboard with Touch ID</a>, and the Magic Keyboard with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> and Numeric Keypad in both <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mjm64ll/a/magic-keyboard-with-touch-id-and-numeric-keypad-for-mac-models-with-apple-silicon-usb-c-us-english-white-keys">white keys</a> and <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mjm74ll/a/magic-keyboard-with-touch-id-and-numeric-keypad-for-mac-models-with-apple-silicon-usb-c-us-english-black-keys">black keys</a>.<br/>
<br/>
The one U.S. English model Apple has not refreshed is the <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mxcj3ll/a/magic-keyboard-with-numeric-keypad-us-english">Magic Keyboard with Numeric Keypad</a>, which lacks &zwnj;Touch ID&zwnj; and continues to use text labels on the same keys.<br/>
<br/>
The change mirrors the one Apple made to its laptops earlier this year, when the new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-air/">MacBook Air</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-neo/">MacBook Neo</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/10/macbook-keyboard-change/">adopted glyphs</a> on the same set of keys.<br/>
<br/>
Since the U.S. English layout is the default option in Canada, Australia, New Zealand, and Singapore, among other countries, the new labeling effectively extends well beyond the United States. Apple has used glyphs on its British English and other European layouts for some time, so the symbols will already be familiar to customers there.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/magic-keyboard/">Magic Keyboard</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-quietly-refreshes-magic-keyboards/">Apple Quietly Refreshes Magic Keyboards</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-quietly-refreshes-magic-keyboards.2487917/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>